==Strategy==
The key to beating Realm of Carnage is to kill the Bores and R.Osts quickly in order to whittle down Hannya's 1 million health before more appear and give you further trouble, all while under constant fire from the extremely damaging attacks. Higher unit levels are generally advantageous. Anti-Reds should be reserved to kill off Bore or damage Hannya while ranged units can take out R.Ost. Try not to let a Bore and a R.Ost stack up together, as that would result in an almost unstoppable pushing force.

Many strategies rely on Bahamut timing to chain and quickly neutralize R.Ost, then pile up as much damage as possible before the next spawns. The Thunderbolt Cannon may be necessary to create a window of opportunity.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]]: Combining high stats and the Strong ability against Reds, Island is an excellent but expensive anti-Red attacker that can support other units. It is recommended to have it at a minimum of level 20+25, as it would be too weak otherwise.
*[[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island]]: A faster and cheaper alternative to its normal equivalent, Manic Island is often centric to the stage. At level 40 with [[True Form]] and some "Strong" Effect UP [[Cat Combo|Combos]], Manic Island can instantly destroy the Ginger Snaches.
*[[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]]: Can effectively stall Hannya because of their humongous health against Red enemies, doubly so in True Form. Their weaken can also help certain units like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] or [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]] to tank extra hits, although it is rather unreliable.
*[[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]]: iCat requires very good timing and either the Move Speed Up [[Talents|talent]] or, with luck, Fried Shrimp's weaken to work. With one of these two options, iCat can rush down Hannya and freeze the boss, giving other units time to get more damage in. Despite his difficulty to use effectively, iCat can still make this stage much more manageable than before if he is able to land a hit. If aided by specific Freeze Combos and Maxed Blood Fruit Treasures, iCat's Freeze can reach 100% uptime, potentially allowing Hannya to be taken down before the first R.Ost could even spawn.
*[[Swordsman Cat (Rare Cat)|Elemental Duelist Cat]]: Can be a very useful asset in rush strategies if boosted to level 33 or higher, as that allows him to survive a hit from a weakened Hannya. A few of them will tear through Hannya quickly. However, his very low range and poor speed leave too much to be desired if Courier is also available.
*[[Cutter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Power Cutter Cat]]: Immune to weaken, extremely fast, survives a lethal strike and strengthens by 400% at 1% health. Quite disposable for how much damage it can easily inflict on the red enemies encountered here.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: Courier is fast, cheap, has a low cooldown and does massive damage to Reds with good stats to begin with. At level 40 with max Blood Fruit Treasures, its damage shoots up to over '''36k''', destroying the Red threats with terrifying ease when used properly. Even Hannya will fall victim to these devastating attacks as Couriers get more and more hits in.
*[[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]]: One of the best meatshields against R.Ost, stalling him to almost a complete halt, allowing your backliners to survive for much longer. At level 40, it can tank 4 hits from the pusher before dying, assuming R.Ost does not land a critical hit. Haniwa's slow movement speed changes little, as you will likely be defending close to your base for the majority of the level. It gets one-shotted by both Hannya and Bore, however.
*[[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Lone Cat and Kitten/Tourist Cat]]: With Resistance/Knockback/Freeze versus traitless enemies, they can disable R.Ost, and make timing Awakened Bahamut extremely simple. They also come from a very easy [[Bombergirl (Deadly)|Advent Stage]] that can be cleared before this.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: With his quick speed and high damage, he can devastate and potentially defeat the R.Ost and potentially take it out if timed well, able to exploit the resultant opening to hit Hannya if he survives.
*[[Fencer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|The Kitty of Liberty]]: While its abilities aren't of any use, The Kitty of Liberty functions similarly to a Dragon variant, and can provide some extra firepower against R.Ost.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: Can Can can crowd-control the Bores and deal good damage to Hannya, it can get double bounty off of Sir Seals. When boosted, it can even hit R.Ost sometimes.
*[[Lieutenant Cat (Special Cat)|Commander Cat]]: A rusher and crowd-controller with Mini-Wave that gives it piercing range, he can be used to allow units such as Awakened Bahamut Cat to land their hits.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Pai-Pai (Uber Rare Cat)|Pai-Pai]]: The designated "counter" to the stage with massive damage/insane resist to reds and weaken immune. Soaks up hits from those reds like no tomorrow and can make short work of both Bore ''and'' Hannya. Her range also allows her to act as support against R.Ost.
*[[Tropical Kalisa (Uber Rare Cat)|Tropical Kalisa]]: Excellent [[:Category:Nuker-class Cats|nuker]] against both Hannya and Bore due to high speed and massive damage against Reds. If timed correctly she can put on some major damage to the boss.
*[[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]]: Only works in True Form, and if upgraded to minimum level 40, preferably with augment from talents. His weaken immunity, disposability and high single-target damage can be used to great effect against Hannya and Bore. At even higher levels, Balrog can also help taking out R.Ost.
*[[Kuu (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kuu γ]]: Strong against reds, has [[Immune to Weaken|Weaken Immunity]] and high damage, able to obliterate both Bore and Hannya, as well as tank hits from any Reds here if her slow attack rate is accounted for.
*[[Momotaro (Uber Rare Cat)|The Peach Devils]]: Can quickly infiltrate into Hannya's range to inflict Freeze, and works well with iCat, despite lacking consistency. They can also provide support against Bore.
*[[Goddess of Light Sirius (Uber Rare Cat)|Goddess of Sunrise Sirius]]: Since you're likely running Strong combos anyway, Sirius gets major improvements to the point where she becomes overpowered, shredding Hannya and the Bore. Also has good DPS against the R. Ost as well.
*[[Thunder Jack (Uber Rare Cat)|Thunder Jack]]: Thunder Jack's high health, speed, and DPS, combined with his Weaken Immunity in his first form, cheap cost, and low cooldown, all can absolutely shred through Hannya's health pool. Just make sure to bring something for the Bore and R.Ost, as they can both deplete his health very quickly if he's not protected, and even protect Hannya from damage due to his Single Targetting.
* [[Knuckles (Uber Rare Cat)|Knuckles]]: Aside from the R. Ost segments, Knuckles demolishes this stage thanks to his high speed, extremely cheap cost for an Uber, and Strong against Red. He can take multiple hits from Hannya, letting him wear her down quickly.
*Any [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] units or other [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|anti-Traitless Cats]]: can quickly take out the R.Ost to give more breathing room. However, if you're using someone like [[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|D'arktanyan]], protect them well so that they don't become complete waste of money.
*[[Mighty Sphinx Korps (Uber Rare Cat)|Hyper Battalion Convoys]]: With their Resistance, Knockback and Weaken against Red, they can easily stall Bore and Hannya and can deal good damage to the R.Ost as well. Although, Hyper Battalion Convoys's Weaken/Knockback is not guaranteed. Also, they are at the pricier side of ubers and have a relatively long recharge, so keep that in mind.

