==Trivia==
*The [[wikipedia:Styx|River Styx]] is a river from Greek Mythology which marks the boundary between the world of the living and the Underworld.
*Although River Styx' and [[The Pure Land (Merciless)|Courts of Torment]]'s Japanese names can both be translated as "Hell Gate" or "Gates of Hell", they don't refer to the same hells: River Styx is spelled with ''jigoku'' (地獄), the generic Japanese word for Hell. Courts of Torment, on the other hand, is ''naraku'' (奈落), which refers to a [[wikipedia:Naraka (Buddhism)|Naraka]], the Buddhist equivalent of Hell.
**Interestingly enough, Hannya's Japanese description mentions that she consumes the souls of those who cannot gain enlightenment, with the term used, ''jōbutsu'' (成仏) specifically referring to attaining Buddhahood.
*In the [[Nyanko Daisensou|Japanese Version]], this is the only Advent Stage whose name does not include the level's difficulty.
*Prior to April 2017 (February 2018 in the [[The Battle Cats|English Version]]), this stage had no known schedule.
*Realm of Carnage was added in the same update as [[Pai-Pai (Uber Rare Cat)|Pai-Pai]], [[Version 5.3 Update|Version 5.3]], as though it was designed specifically for her to counter.
* The enemy base's HP is composed of two 666s, believed to be the "[[wikipedia:Number of the Beast|Number of the Beast]]".
*This is the second advent stage to be added in The Battle Cats Unite! as it was distributed in the [[The Battle Cats Unite!/Patch 1.0.7 Update#December 15, 2023 Update Patch|December 15, 2023 Update Patch]].

